<!--
    The `in` glyph from docs/assets/buk-in.svg, which is the app's mark.

    108x108dp layers. The glyph is fitted to a **52dp** box, not the 66dp safe zone: 66dp is
    the largest content that is guaranteed not to be *cut off*, which is a different thing
    from the largest content that should be *drawn*. At 66dp the mark filled the whole safe
    square, broke out of the 66dp safe circle at its corners, and sat visibly tighter in its
    mask than every neighbouring icon on the launcher. 52dp puts it inside the 60dp keyline
    circle with even margin, which is where a product mark belongs.

    Coordinates are baked rather than applied through a <group> transform: VectorDrawable
    group transform order is easy to get subtly wrong and impossible to see until it is on a
    launcher. They are rounded to two decimals, which is past visible at this size and is
    what keeps the longest path under aapt2's 32 KB string limit — over it, the path data is
    silently replaced with STRING_TOO_LARGE and the icon renders empty.
-->
